# shellcheck shell=sh disable=SC2034
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  NoporIS — dual-persona bridge posture (operator config sample)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  ⚠  HONESTY: this configures NoporIS, the guarded BRIDGE between two personas
#     on ONE stock-Android handset. It is an APP on stock Android. It is NEVER
#     "Postern OS", never Porog (the container), never a "Seal". Its isolation is
#     Android's own work-profile mechanism, configured by an unprivileged app —
#     only as strong as the kernel underneath it.
#
#     The GOOGLE-PLAY PERSONA is the LESS-PRIVATE side, by construction. A
#     persona running Google Play Services (GMS) phones home to Google. NoporIS
#     sells SEPARATION + CONVENIENCE, not privacy on that side. It cannot make a
#     Google-Android persona private, cannot give it a separate hardware
#     identity, and cannot hide the device from Google.
#
#     A rooted / unlocked / kernel-compromised host DEFEATS the separation.
#     UNAUDITED reference-prototype (DESIGN ONLY, not yet staffed); attests
#     NOTHING. Play Integrity STRONG fails on both personas by design. The coin
#     is worthless and is not a security. Personal use is free. Not legal advice.
#
#  Copy to one of (first match wins):
#     ~/.config/noporis/noporis.conf
#     /etc/noporis/noporis.conf
#  Sourced as POSIX sh (KEY=VALUE). Anything you don't set keeps the private,
#  default-safe value baked in. Defaults are the MOST-CONTAINED choice.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Trust tier. FIXED, not an input. NoporIS is on stock Android; nothing here
#     is attestable. There is no measured-boot roothash of a persona. Leave it.
#       non-attestable   the only honest value; do not change
NIS_TIER=non-attestable

# --- Isolation mechanism for the second persona. NoporIS does NOT own this — it
#     configures Android's own DevicePolicyManager. The fence is real but it is
#     Android's, not Postern's, and only as strong as the shared kernel.
#       WORK_PROFILE   AOSP managed profile (user 10+): the realistic NoporIS
#       APP_CLONE      OEM dual-apps / cloning (often weaker, per-app only)
#     Waydroid-style guest userland is OUT OF SCOPE for stock Android — that is
#     the apps/sloboda escape hatch, a different product.
NIS_MECHANISM=WORK_PROFILE

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CLEAN PERSONA — the Google-vs-Google-free choice.
#  A USER-SELECTABLE CONFIG INPUT, never hardcoded to Google. Default is the
#  private, Google-free base. These are OPTIONS with real trade-offs
#  (compatibility vs contained), NOT promises. NONE unlock integrity-gated apps:
#  banking / Wallet / DRM still refuse — STRONG fails regardless of this choice.
#       VANILLA  AOSP, no Google, no microG   most private, least compatible
#                                             (many mainstream apps degrade)
#       MICROG   Google-free re-implementation  most apps work; FCM/maps/sign-in
#                                             relayed. Recommended when you want
#                                             compatibility with less Google.
#                                             Honest limit: microG still contacts
#                                             Google's servers for what it relays
#                                             and can't reliably pass Play
#                                             Integrity — no rescue for banking.
#       GAPPS    Google Play Services         least private; plants Google's
#                                             blobs in the persona. Still won't
#                                             pass STRONG — little gain.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NIS_CLEAN_PERSONA_SYSTEM_TYPE=VANILLA

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  GOOGLE-PLAY PERSONA — the LESS-PRIVATE side, off by default.
#  Turning this on creates a Google-Android persona that talks to Google: your
#  Google account, device + hardware identifiers, installed-app inventory, and
#  (with permission) location leave the device. NoporIS gives this persona a
#  SEPARATE BOX for its data and accounts — not a separate phone, and not
#  privacy. If a thing would be unsafe for Google to see, don't do it here.
#       0  no Google persona (default)
#       1  create the less-private Google-Play persona (EXPLICIT opt-in)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NIS_GOOGLE_PERSONA_ENABLED=0

# --- Route the Google persona's egress separately (e.g. a distinct VPN/exit).
#     HONESTY: even routed elsewhere, device-wide hardware identity still
#     correlates the two personas — same SIM/IMEI/serial, one physical device.
#     This reduces NETWORK correlation only; it does not hide the device.
#       0  share the clean side's network (default; personas correlate by IP)
#       1  attempt separate egress for the Google persona
NIS_GOOGLE_PERSONA_SEPARATE_EGRESS=0

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CROSS-PERSONA BRIDGES — clipboard, contacts, files sharing between personas.
#  DENY-BY-DEFAULT. Everything here starts OFF. Each bridge is a hole you open on
#  purpose; turn it off when you're done. Anything but the literal value below is
#  treated as OFF. NoporIS never opens a bridge you didn't open.
#       0  closed (default)   1  open (explicit)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NIS_BRIDGE_CLIPBOARD=0
NIS_BRIDGE_CONTACTS=0
NIS_BRIDGE_FILES=0

# --- Consent-gate bridge state file. OWNED BY THE CONSENT-GATE COMPONENT.
#     NoporIS only READS it and treats anything but a first line of exactly
#     "enabled" as OFF. Do NOT point this at a file NoporIS can write — the whole
#     point is that the bridge cannot open itself.
# NIS_BRIDGE_STATE=/run/noporis/consent/persona-bridge.state

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  BADGE / ATTESTATION DISPLAY POSTURE. See badges.json for the full rules.
#  Attestation is shown ONLY where it is true. On stock Android it never is, so a
#  padlock / "attested" / "verified" badge is NEVER rendered for either persona.
#  The Google persona is badged "less private", never a padlock it hasn't earned.
#       strict  render attestation badges only where genuinely true (default)
#     There is no other honest setting; this key exists to be auditable, not
#     tunable. A relaxed mode would over-claim, so it is not offered.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NIS_BADGE_MODE=strict
